<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Ode to the Socialist Motherland</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1968</span><span class="sg-chain-h">new words (Cultural Revolution version)</span></li><li><a href="/songs/the-east-is-red">The East Is Red (stage work)</a> <span class="sg-chain-y">1964</span><span class="sg-chain-h">closing number</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Farewell My Concubine (film)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1993</span><span class="sg-chain-h">heard in</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Beijing Olympics opening ceremony arrangement (Chen Qigang)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2008</span><span class="sg-chain-h">new arrangement and words</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Xinwen Lianbo theme (Meng Weidong)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">its opening inspired by the song's first phrase</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Musical road, Fengtai District, Beijing</span><span class="sg-chain-h">plays the melody</span></li></ul></section>
